# Raw assets — ignored BY DEFAULT, not by rule.
#
# The point of this block is to stop UNWANTED EXPOSURE: a sibling project
# leaked real reference photos and an account cache onto a public branch, and
# the fix was to stop sweeping whole directories into commits. It was never
# meant to block recordkeeping, and it should not be read that way.
#
# So the default is ignore, and anything irreplaceable is explicitly kept
# below. The test is simple: if losing the file means the work cannot be
# rebuilt, it belongs in the repo. If it can be re-downloaded or regenerated,
# it does not.
#
# NOTE the pattern is `/assets/*` and not `/assets/` — git will not descend
# into an excluded DIRECTORY, so the negations underneath would silently do
# nothing.
#
# Anchored to repo root (leading slash) — composed game-ready output lives in
# src/assets/ (a different directory, also named "assets") and IS committed.
/assets/*

# KEPT — irreplaceable. prodbyKCTW's own voice: the recording the stomp is cut
# from. It exists nowhere else but his phone, and tools/make_sfx.py cannot
# rebuild the punches without it. Committed with his explicit permission.
!/assets/sfx-src/
/assets/sfx-src/*
!/assets/sfx-src/kctw-punches.m4a
!/assets/sfx-src/README.md

# KEPT — irreplaceable. The v1 SIDESCROLLER export. Regenerating these means
# paying AutoSprite credits again and risking a different result;
# tools/compose_player_sheet.py cannot run without them.
# prodbyKCTW's logo — a brand mark, not made here and not regenerable. Same
# rule as the voice memo: if losing it means the work cannot be rebuilt, keep
# it. The end credits cannot ship without it.
!/assets/brand/
!/assets/raw-sprites/
# CLIENT REFERENCE ART. Every one of these arrived as a chat attachment and
# existed NOWHERE else — not on disk, not in Drive, not re-downloadable. They
# had to be recovered out of the session transcript's base64. That is the
# textbook case for the rule above: if losing it means the work cannot be
# rebuilt, commit it. Losing these means asking the client to send them again.
!/assets/refs/

# Claude Code project settings — local only, never shared via the repo.
#
# ...except the one skill that IS this project's work. The multiplane cutter
# and its SAM pass were developed here and the client asked for them to be
# kept; losing them means rebuilding the whole backdrop pipeline from the
# commit log. Same test as /assets/* above: if losing it means the work
# cannot be rebuilt, commit it.
#
# And the same STAR PATTERN, for the same reason — `.claude/` excludes the
# directory itself, and git will not descend into an excluded directory to
# find a negation inside it. Each level has to be opened before the next one
# can be re-excluded. Writing `.claude/` with a `!` under it silently keeps
# ignoring everything, which is how this was first written.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.claude/skills/*
# ⚠️ EVERY OWNED SKILL NEEDS ITS OWN LINE HERE. The negation is per-directory,
# so a new skill written into .claude/skills/ is silently ignored until it is
# listed — which is exactly what happened to the two below: they were written,
# `git add`ed, and did not appear in `git status` at all.
!.claude/skills/backdrop-multiplane/
!.claude/skills/game-harness/
!.claude/skills/contest-leaderboard/

# INSTALLED SKILLS ARE NOT PART OF THIS GAME.
#
# A skill installer wrote 30 third-party design skills (and its lockfile) into
# .agents/, and they were swept into a commit that was supposed to be one
# render file — 604K of Tailwind/shadcn/brand-kit guidance sitting in a repo
# for a canvas pixel-art platformer that imports none of it. The client's
# note was explicit: those screenshots were a list of skills to INSTALL, not
# material to add to this build.
#
# This is the exact drift CLAUDE.md opens by warning about — the Jandé repo
# accumulated a Phaser scaffold and two Godot projects the same way. Skills
# belong to the account that installed them, not to the game.
.agents/
skills-lock.json

# Local capture/debug output
tools/captures/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Playwright harness screenshots. Written into the repo root by the
# scratchpad scripts (day/night sweeps, stage proofs) and regenerated on
# every run — verification output, not source. Ignored rather than tidied
# away by hand because the thing that must never happen on this project is
# harness output riding into a commit unnoticed; see the top of CLAUDE.md.
shots/

# Cloudflare
.wrangler/
cloudflare/.wrangler/

# The loop bench is generated for a deploy, never committed: it is ~12MB of
# his instrumental masters and the tool exists for about a week. See
# tools/build_loopbench.py.
/public/bench/
